config BR2_PACKAGE_RETRO_ZERO
	bool "retro-zero"
	depends on BR2_INSTALL_LIBSTDCPP
	select BR2_PACKAGE_ALSA_LIB
	help
	  Retro-Zero is a Libretro frontend with an LVGL user interface,
	  designed for small handhelds. It draws through /dev/fb0, so unlike
	  RetroArch it needs no GPU, no KMS and no EGL: on this GPU-less
	  board it runs entirely on the framebuffer.

	  It loads the same libretro cores as RetroArch, so enable the
	  cores you want (BR2_PACKAGE_LIBRETRO_*) alongside it.

	  Upstream: https://github.com/geo-tp/Retro-Zero

	  Note: upstream ships no LICENSE file, so the code is
	  all-rights-reserved by default. See package/retro-zero/README.md
	  before redistributing.

comment "retro-zero needs a toolchain w/ C++"
	depends on !BR2_INSTALL_LIBSTDCPP

if BR2_PACKAGE_RETRO_ZERO

config BR2_PACKAGE_RETRO_ZERO_CONSOLE
	bool "retro-zero console integration"
	help
	  Install the files that make Retro-Zero the system's front-end on a
	  dedicated console: an init script that starts it at boot, and a
	  supervisor that restarts it whenever it exits so the device never
	  falls back to a blank framebuffer. Also creates the ROM and save
	  directories.

	  Only enable this on a device dedicated to Retro-Zero. It assumes
	  the root filesystem is writable for saves.

endif
